# Pageflex Architecture

When refactoring User, Group, or Permission logic, follow this Schema-First approach:

## 1. Schema Separation
- **UserGroups** = Storefront access (which products can this user see?)
- **AdminGroups** = Dashboard access (what buttons can this user click?)
- User has many-to-many with both via UserGroupMember and AdminGroupMember

## 2. AdminGroup Permission Flags
AdminGroup must have explicit boolean flags:
- `canApproveOrders`
- `canManageInventory`
- `canEditUsers`

Keep `permissions` JSON for flexible extras.

## 3. Middleware
- `requireAdmin`: User is admin if `isAdmin=true` OR has any AdminGroup
- Attach `req.user.permissions` from AdminGroup flags (union across all groups)
- Use `requirePermission('canApproveOrders')` for route-level checks

## 4. Product Filtering (Catalog Restriction)
- If user logged in: filter products by their UserGroup (groupId in allowedGroupIds)
- If no group: show "Public" (groupId null) only
- Admins see all

## 5. Permission Manager UI
- Left: list of AdminGroups (click to select)
- Right: Permission Matrix with toggles (Approvals, Inventory, Users)
- Below: list of Users in group with Add/Remove search bar
